% Lower Limb Prostheses: LCD L33787 and its Policy Article A52496 (DME
% MACs). A policy program of the DMEPOS model: it includes dmepos.le (orders,
% delivery, benefit category, continued need, the prior authorization list)
% and states when a claim for a lower limb prosthesis or one of its
% components is REASONABLE AND NECESSARY:
%   - a prosthesis (the prosthetic systems the Article's coding guidelines
%     name: partial foot L5000–L5020, immediate post-operative L5400–L5460,
%     initial L5500, L5505, preparatory L5510–L5600, exoskeletal L5100–L5280,
%     endoskeletal L5301–L5341): the beneficiary will reach or maintain a
%     defined functional state within a reasonable period of time, is
%     motivated to ambulate, and has a potential functional level above 0;
%   - a component whose coverage the LCD ties to the functional level (the
%     table llp_levels, one row per code with its passage): the feet (level
%     1: L5970, L5974; level 2: L5972, L5978; level 3: L5973, L5976, L5979,
%     L5980, L5981, L5987), the knees (level 1: the other knee systems;
%     level 3: the fluid and pneumatic knees, the fluid control addition
%     L5848 and the microprocessor knees L5856, L5857, L5858; level 4: the
%     high activity frame L5930), the axial rotation units (level 2: L5982,
%     L5984, L5985, L5986), the polycentric hip joint (level 3: L5961) — the
%     prosthesis's criteria met, the level reached, and the component not one
%     the LCD denies with an initial or preparatory prosthesis;
%   - a fluid, pneumatic or microprocessor knee at level 2, under the LCD's
%     criteria 1–3 (and 1–4 for a microprocessor knee); a level 3 foot at
%     level 2 with such a knee, when the knee requires it;
%   - the powered flexion/extension assist L5859: a microprocessor knee
%     L5856 on the prosthesis, level 3 only, a documented comorbidity of the
%     spine or sound limb, daily charging, alerts.
% Never covered (no rule concludes them): the powered ankle addition L5969,
% the user-adjustable heel height L5990, any prosthesis at level 0. The
% prosthetic donning sleeve (L7600) is statutorily noncovered: in scope, in
% no benefit. The benefit is not durable medical equipment: the Policy
% Article places lower limb prostheses under the Medicare Artificial Legs,
% Arms and Eyes benefit (Social Security Act §1861(s)(9)) — the constant
% "artificial legs, arms and eyes" of eye_prostheses.le.
%
% How the criteria are read. The functional level is a NUMBER, 0 to 4 (the
% K0–K4 of the LCD): the level the clinical assessment of the treating
% practitioner and the prosthetist designates, a fact of the record —
% level 0 cannot ambulate or transfer safely, 1 is the household ambulator
% at fixed cadence, 2 the limited community ambulator over low barriers, 3
% the community ambulator at variable cadence, 4 the high impact user (the
% LCD's "Clinical assessments of beneficiary rehabilitation potential").
% The thresholds are in the table. What else the record states is a
% scenario fact: the clinical evaluation of the functional level, what the
% knee is indicated for and whether it recovers from a stumble, the daily
% charging and the alerts, a comorbidity (the shared template "the medical
% record of B documents C"). The findings this policy reads (the judged
% template of dmepos.le), and the criterion each stands for:
%   functional state reachable (will reach or maintain a defined functional
%   state within a reasonable period of time); motivated to ambulate;
%   advanced knee system justified (a level 2 fluid, pneumatic or
%   microprocessor knee, criterion 2: how the knee will improve the
%   functional health outcomes and the activities of daily living, and that
%   lower-level knee systems were considered and ruled out — ONE finding);
%   higher level foot required (a level 3 foot at level 2: required for the
%   safe and proper use of the prescribed knee system).
% A component is an accessory (the shared template) of the prosthesis it is
% part of; the prosthesis's HCPCS code tells whether it is initial or
% preparatory.
%
% The payment conditions the Policy Article adds ("Policy specific
% documentation requirements"), in section remedy: the prosthetist's
% records hold information about the beneficiary's history and current
% condition supporting the designated functional level ("The simple entry
% of a K-level modifier in those records is not sufficient"); for a foot or
% a knee, the records document the functional need for its technologic or
% design feature. The microprocessor knees, the microprocessor ankle L5973
% and the feet L5980, L5987 are on the prior authorization list (dmepos.le);
% no lower limb prosthesis is on the face-to-face list.
%
% Not modelled: the socket components (test sockets, inserts, replacement
% sockets L5700–L5703), covers, suspension and the other additions the LCD
% covers "in accordance with the functional level assessment" without a
% level of their own; the exceptions "considered in an individual case"; the
% latitude for bilateral amputees; repairs, adjustments and replacements;
% the hospital and SNF payment rules; the K-level, KX, GA, GY, GZ, RT and LT
% modifiers; the PDAC coding verification.

the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    % the record
    the functional level of *a beneficiary* is *a number*; undefined.
    *a beneficiary* had a clinical evaluation to determine the functional level; undefined.
    *an item* is indicated for functional level *a number*; undefined.
    *an item* detects a stumble of the user and stabilizes the knee unit; undefined.
    *a beneficiary* is able to make use of a product that requires daily charging; undefined.
    *a beneficiary* is able to understand and respond to error alerts of the unit; undefined.
    the records of the prosthetist support the functional level designated for *a beneficiary*; undefined.
    the records document the functional need for the design feature of *an item*; undefined.
    % the codes and the lists
    the minimum functional level for code *a code* is *a number* under table llp_levels.
    *a condition* is a comorbidity qualifying for a powered knee assist.
    code *a code* is excluded from the artificial limbs benefit.
    % derived
    *an item* is a lower limb prosthesis.
    *an item* is an advanced knee component.
    *an item* is a microprocessor knee.
    *an item* is a level three foot.
    *an item* is a foot or knee component.
    *an item* is excluded with the prosthesis *a device*.
    *a beneficiary* meets the lower limb prosthesis criteria.
    *a beneficiary* has a potential functional level above zero.
    *a component* is covered at the functional level of *a beneficiary*.
    *a beneficiary* meets the level two criteria for the advanced knee *an item*.
    the microprocessor knee criteria of level two are met for *an item*.
    the functional level documentation is met for *a beneficiary*.
    the design feature documentation is met for *an item*.

% The functional level each component needs (LCD L33787): its minimum
% level, row by row with the passage.
