the knowledge base lower_limb_prostheses includes these resources:
    dmepos.

the knowledge base lower_limb_prostheses includes:

LCD L33787 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/lcd.aspx?lcdid=33787".
the text of LCD L33787 is at "sources/lcd/L33787.txt".
Policy Article A52496 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/article.aspx?articleid=52496".
the text of Policy Article A52496 is at "sources/article/A52496.txt".

% What the prostheses are, by code (the Article's coding guidelines).
rule llp_partial_foot with provenance Policy Article A52496,
        confer "Codes L5000, L5010, and L5020 describe products that are necessary for standing balance and toe off support in beneficiaries who are missing the forefoot or digits":
an item is a lower limb prosthesis
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["L5000", "L5010", "L5020"].

rule llp_immediate with provenance Policy Article A52496,
        confer "L5450 and L5460 describe non-weight bearing rigid dressings that are immediate post-surgical or early fitting":
an item is a lower limb prosthesis
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["L5400", "L5410", "L5420", "L5430", "L5450", "L5460"].

rule llp_initial with provenance Policy Article A52496,
        confer "Initial L5500 and L5505 describe prosthetic systems which are used during the initial stages of prosthetic limb use":
an item is a lower limb prosthesis
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["L5500", "L5505"].

rule llp_preparatory with provenance Policy Article A52496,
        confer "Preparatory L5510, L5520, L5530, L5535, L5540, L5560, L5570, L5580, L5585, L5590, L5595, and L5600 describe preparatory prosthetic limb systems":
an item is a lower limb prosthesis
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["L5510", "L5520", "L5530", "L5535", "L5540", "L5560", "L5570", "L5580", "L5585", "L5590", "L5595", "L5600"].

rule llp_exoskeletal with provenance Policy Article A52496,
        confer "Exoskeletal L5100, L5105, L5150, L5160, L5200, L5250, L5270, and L5280 describe exoskeleton prosthetic limb systems":
an item is a lower limb prosthesis
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["L5100", "L5105", "L5150", "L5160", "L5200", "L5250", "L5270", "L5280"].

rule llp_endoskeletal with provenance Policy Article A52496,
        confer "Endoskeletal L5301, L5312, L5321, L5331, and L5341 describe endoskeletal prosthetic systems":
an item is a lower limb prosthesis
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["L5301", "L5312", "L5321", "L5331", "L5341"].

% The knees the LCD covers at level 2 under limited circumstances, and the
% microprocessor knees among them.
rule llp_advanced_knee with provenance LCD L33787,
        confer "is also covered under limited circumstances for beneficiaries whose functional level is 2, when all of the following criteria (1-3) are met":
an item is an advanced knee component
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["L5610", "L5613", "L5614", "L5615", "L5722", "L5724", "L5726", "L5728", "L5780", "L5814", "L5822", "L5824", "L5826", "L5828", "L5830", "L5840", "L5841", "L5848", "L5856", "L5857", "L5858"].

rule llp_microprocessor_knee with provenance LCD L33787,
        confer "In addition, for coverage of an electronic/microprocessor-controlled knee system (L5856, L5857, or L5858 plus associated components) for beneficiaries whose functional level is 2, all of the following criteria (1-4) must also be met":
an item is a microprocessor knee
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["L5856", "L5857", "L5858"].

rule llp_level_three_foot with provenance LCD L33787,
        confer "A microprocessor-controlled ankle foot system (L5973), energy storing foot (L5976), dynamic response foot with multi-axial ankle (L5979), flex foot system (L5980), flex-walk system or equal (L5981), or shank foot system with vertical loading pylon (L5987) is covered when one of the following criteria is met":
an item is a level three foot
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["L5973", "L5976", "L5979", "L5980", "L5981", "L5987"].

% The feet and knees whose design feature needs its functional need
% documented (section remedy reads this).
rule llp_foot_or_knee with provenance LCD L33787,
        confer "Coverage is extended only if there is sufficient clinical documentation of functional need for the technologic or design feature of a given type of knee":
an item is a foot or knee component
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["L5970", "L5972", "L5973", "L5974", "L5976", "L5978", "L5979", "L5980", "L5981", "L5987", "L5610", "L5611", "L5613", "L5614", "L5615", "L5616", "L5710", "L5711", "L5712", "L5714", "L5716", "L5718", "L5722", "L5724", "L5726", "L5728", "L5780", "L5810", "L5811", "L5812", "L5814", "L5816", "L5818", "L5822", "L5824", "L5826", "L5828", "L5830", "L5840", "L5841", "L5848", "L5856", "L5857", "L5858", "L5859", "L5930"].

% The components the LCD denies with an initial or preparatory prosthesis.
rule llp_excluded_below_knee with provenance LCD L33787,
        confer "When an initial below knee prosthesis (L5500) or a preparatory below knee prosthesis (L5510, L5520, L5530, L5540) is provided, prosthetic substitutions and/or additions of procedures and components are covered in accordance with the functional level assessment except for codes L5629, L5638, L5639, L5646, L5647, L5704, L5785, L5962, and L5980 which will be denied as not reasonable and necessary":
an item is excluded with the prosthesis a device
    if the HCPCS code of the device is a code
    and the code is in ["L5500", "L5510", "L5520", "L5530", "L5540"]
    and the HCPCS code of the item is an other code
    and the other code is in ["L5629", "L5638", "L5639", "L5646", "L5647", "L5704", "L5785", "L5962", "L5980"].

rule llp_excluded_below_knee_prefabricated with provenance LCD L33787,
        confer "When a below knee preparatory prefabricated prosthesis (L5535) is provided, prosthetic substitutions and/or additions of procedures are covered in accordance with the functional level assessment except for codes L5620, L5629, L5645, L5646, L5670, L5676, L5704, and L5962 which will be denied as not reasonable and necessary":
an item is excluded with the prosthesis a device
    if the HCPCS code of the device is "L5535"
    and the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["L5620", "L5629", "L5645", "L5646", "L5670", "L5676", "L5704", "L5962"].

rule llp_excluded_above_knee with provenance LCD L33787,
        confer "When an above knee initial prosthesis (L5505) or an above knee preparatory (L5560, L5570, L5580, L5590, L5595, L5600) prosthesis is provided":
an item is excluded with the prosthesis a device
    if the HCPCS code of the device is a code
    and the code is in ["L5505", "L5560", "L5570", "L5580", "L5590", "L5595", "L5600"]
    and the HCPCS code of the item is an other code
    and the other code is in ["L5610", "L5631", "L5640", "L5642", "L5644", "L5648", "L5705", "L5706", "L5964", "L5980", "L5710", "L5711", "L5712", "L5714", "L5716", "L5718", "L5722", "L5724", "L5726", "L5728", "L5780", "L5790", "L5795"].

rule llp_excluded_above_knee_prefabricated with provenance LCD L33787,
        confer "When an above knee preparatory prefabricated prosthesis (L5585) is provided, prosthetic substitution and/or additions of procedures and components are covered in accordance with the functional level assessment except for codes L5624, L5631, L5648, L5651, L5652, L5705, L5706, L5964, and L5966 which will be denied as not reasonable and necessary":
an item is excluded with the prosthesis a device
    if the HCPCS code of the device is "L5585"
    and the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["L5624", "L5631", "L5648", "L5651", "L5652", "L5705", "L5706", "L5964", "L5966"].

% The comorbidities L5859 needs.
comorbidity of the spine affecting hip extension is a comorbidity qualifying for a powered knee assist,
    as stated in LCD L33787, confer "Has a documented comorbidity of the spine and/or sound limb affecting hip extension and/or quadriceps function that impairs K3 level function with the use of a microprocessor-controlled knee alone".
comorbidity of the spine affecting quadriceps function is a comorbidity qualifying for a powered knee assist,
    as stated in LCD L33787, confer "Has a documented comorbidity of the spine and/or sound limb affecting hip extension and/or quadriceps function that impairs K3 level function with the use of a microprocessor-controlled knee alone".
comorbidity of the sound limb affecting hip extension is a comorbidity qualifying for a powered knee assist,
    as stated in LCD L33787, confer "Has a documented comorbidity of the spine and/or sound limb affecting hip extension and/or quadriceps function that impairs K3 level function with the use of a microprocessor-controlled knee alone".
comorbidity of the sound limb affecting quadriceps function is a comorbidity qualifying for a powered knee assist,
    as stated in LCD L33787, confer "Has a documented comorbidity of the spine and/or sound limb affecting hip extension and/or quadriceps function that impairs K3 level function with the use of a microprocessor-controlled knee alone".

section applicability is:

% The codes this policy decides: the prostheses, the components with a
% functional level, L5859, the never-covered L5969 and L5990, the donning
% sleeve the Article denies.
rule llp_codes with provenance Policy Article A52496,
        confer "Lower limb prostheses are covered under the Medicare Artificial Legs, Arms and Eyes benefit (Social Security Act §1861(s)(9))":
the policy for code a code is lower_limb_prostheses
    if the code is in ["L5000", "L5010", "L5020", "L5100", "L5105", "L5150", "L5160", "L5200", "L5250", "L5270", "L5280", "L5301", "L5312", "L5321", "L5331", "L5341", "L5400", "L5410", "L5420", "L5430", "L5450", "L5460", "L5500", "L5505", "L5510", "L5520", "L5530", "L5535", "L5540", "L5560", "L5570", "L5580", "L5585", "L5590", "L5595", "L5600", "L5610", "L5611", "L5613", "L5614", "L5615", "L5616", "L5710", "L5711", "L5712", "L5714", "L5716", "L5718", "L5722", "L5724", "L5726", "L5728", "L5780", "L5810", "L5811", "L5812", "L5814", "L5816", "L5818", "L5822", "L5824", "L5826", "L5828", "L5830", "L5840", "L5841", "L5848", "L5856", "L5857", "L5858", "L5859", "L5930", "L5961", "L5969", "L5970", "L5972", "L5973", "L5974", "L5976", "L5978", "L5979", "L5980", "L5981", "L5982", "L5984", "L5985", "L5986", "L5987", "L5990", "L7600"].

% The benefit: the Artificial Legs, Arms and Eyes benefit of Social Security
% Act §1861(s)(9) — for every code but the donning sleeve.
rule llp_benefit with provenance Policy Article A52496,
        confer "Lower limb prostheses are covered under the Medicare Artificial Legs, Arms and Eyes benefit (Social Security Act §1861(s)(9))":
the benefit category of code a code is "artificial legs, arms and eyes"
    if the policy for code the code is lower_limb_prostheses
    and it is not the case that
        code the code is excluded from the artificial limbs benefit.

code "L7600" is excluded from the artificial limbs benefit,
    as stated in Policy Article A52496, confer "A prosthetic donning sleeve (L7600) will be denied as noncovered".

section question is:

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The prosthesis.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule llp_prosthesis with provenance LCD L33787,
        confer "A lower limb prosthesis is covered when the beneficiary":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is a lower limb prosthesis
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary meets the lower limb prosthesis criteria.

rule llp_criteria with provenance LCD L33787,
        confer "Will reach or maintain a defined functional state within a reasonable period of time; and Is motivated to ambulate":
a beneficiary meets the lower limb prosthesis criteria
    if the finding functional state reachable about the beneficiary is established
    and the finding motivated to ambulate about the beneficiary is established
    and the beneficiary has a potential functional level above zero.

rule llp_level_zero with provenance LCD L33787,
        confer "Prostheses will be denied as not reasonable and necessary if the beneficiary’s potential functional level is 0":
a beneficiary has a potential functional level above zero
    if the functional level of the beneficiary is a number
    and the number >= 1.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The components: the level the table gives, with the prosthesis's
% criteria met and the component not denied with its prosthesis.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule llp_component with provenance LCD L33787,
        confer "If a prosthesis is denied as not reasonable and necessary, related additions will also be denied as not reasonable and necessary":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is an accessory of a device
    and the device is a lower limb prosthesis
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary meets the lower limb prosthesis criteria
    and the item is covered at the functional level of the beneficiary
    and it is not the case that
        the item is excluded with the prosthesis the device.

rule llp_component_level with provenance LCD L33787,
        confer "Other prosthetic knees are considered for coverage based upon functional classification":
a component is covered at the functional level of a beneficiary
    if the HCPCS code of the component is a code
    and the minimum functional level for code the code is a number under table llp_levels
    and the functional level of the beneficiary is an other number
    and the other number >= the number.

% A fluid, pneumatic or microprocessor knee at level 2 (criteria 1-3, and
% 1-4 for a microprocessor knee).
rule llp_knee_level_two with provenance LCD L33787,
        confer "is also covered under limited circumstances for beneficiaries whose functional level is 2, when all of the following criteria (1-3) are met":
a component is covered at the functional level of a beneficiary
    if the component is an advanced knee component
    and the functional level of the beneficiary is 2
    and the beneficiary meets the level two criteria for the advanced knee the component.

rule llp_knee_level_two_criteria with provenance LCD L33787,
        confer "The beneficiary has had a clinical evaluation to determine their functional level":
a beneficiary meets the level two criteria for the advanced knee an item
    if the beneficiary had a clinical evaluation to determine the functional level
    and the finding advanced knee system justified about the beneficiary is established
    and the microprocessor knee criteria of level two are met for the item.

rule llp_microprocessor_level_two with provenance LCD L33787,
        confer "The electronic/microprocessor knee has integrated technology that allows the knee to detect when the user trips or stumbles and can automatically adjust to stabilize the knee unit":
the microprocessor knee criteria of level two are met for an item
    if the item is a microprocessor knee
    and the item is indicated for functional level 2
    and the item detects a stumble of the user and stabilizes the knee unit
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary is able to make use of a product that requires daily charging
    and the beneficiary is able to understand and respond to error alerts of the unit.

% a fluid or pneumatic knee has no criteria 1-4: a device of this model
rule llp_not_microprocessor:
the microprocessor knee criteria of level two are met for an item
    if the item is an advanced knee component
    and it is not the case that
        the item is a microprocessor knee.

% A level 3 foot at level 2: with a knee covered at level 2, when the knee
% requires the foot.
rule llp_foot_level_two with provenance LCD L33787,
        confer "A higher-level (i.e., functional level 3) foot is required for the safe and proper use of the prescribed knee system":
a component is covered at the functional level of a beneficiary
    if the component is a level three foot
    and the functional level of the beneficiary is 2
    and the component is an accessory of a device
    and an other component is an accessory of the device
    and the other component is an advanced knee component
    and the beneficiary meets the level two criteria for the advanced knee the other component
    and the finding higher level foot required about the beneficiary is established.

% The powered flexion/extension assist (L5859).
rule llp_powered_assist with provenance LCD L33787,
        confer "is only covered when the beneficiary meets all of the criteria below":
a component is covered at the functional level of a beneficiary
    if the HCPCS code of the component is "L5859"
    and the component is an accessory of a device
    and an other component is an accessory of the device
    and the HCPCS code of the other component is "L5856"
    and the functional level of the beneficiary is 3
    and the medical record of the beneficiary documents a condition
    and the condition is a comorbidity qualifying for a powered knee assist
    and the beneficiary is able to make use of a product that requires daily charging
    and the beneficiary is able to understand and respond to error alerts of the unit.

section remedy is:

% The policy's own conditions of payment (Policy Article A52496, "Policy
% specific documentation requirements").
rule llp_documentation with provenance Policy Article A52496,
        confer "Functional ability information must be clearly documented and retained in the prosthetist's records":
the policy specific documentation requirements are met for a claim
    if the policy of the claim is lower_limb_prostheses
    and the claim is for an item
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the functional level documentation is met for the beneficiary
    and the design feature documentation is met for the item.

rule llp_level_documentation with provenance Policy Article A52496,
        confer "There must be information about the beneficiary’s history and current condition which supports the designation of the functional level by the prosthetist":
the functional level documentation is met for a beneficiary
    if the records of the prosthetist support the functional level designated for the beneficiary.

rule llp_feature_documentation with provenance LCD L33787,
        confer "Coverage is extended only if there is sufficient clinical documentation of functional need for the technologic or design feature of a given type of foot":
the design feature documentation is met for an item
    if the item is a foot or knee component
    and the records document the functional need for the design feature of the item.

% a prosthesis or another component: a device of this model
rule llp_no_feature_documentation:
the design feature documentation is met for an item
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and it is not the case that
        the item is a foot or knee component.
